#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
khaos-lab — central control panel for the arc toolkit.
Renamed twice 2026-08-26 (control panel -> khaos-panel -> khaos-klinik ->
khaos-lab), user's own call each time -- keep it simple stuck.

A lightweight GUI front-end over the `arc` CLI you already have. Every button
shells out to the same `arc <subcommand>` (or a small handful of raw commands
for live status) already built and running on this machine -- this does not
reimplement logic, it's a dashboard/launcher over what already works. The one
exception is reading generated JSON (khaos-lab/inventory/inventory.json) for
the Inventory view.

Manual-start only, same principle as arc-break/arc-pine/darkstat/zap -- no
autostart entry, nothing brings this up on its own.

Layout: left sidebar picks a category, right side shows that category's view,
bottom is a shared output console (every action's real stdout/stderr lands
there).

Structure (rewritten class-based 2026-09-19 -- it used to be one 1,300-line
main() of nested closures, which is where most of its bugs came from):

  Runner        the ONE way commands run: output to a temp file (never a pipe a
                stray grandchild can hold open), own process group so a timeout
                kills the whole tree, stdin closed so nothing waits on a TTY.
  UiBridge      worker threads NEVER touch Tk; they post callables here and the
                main thread runs them (Tkinter isn't thread-safe).
  Poller        named periodic jobs: exactly one chain per name, an in-flight
                guard (a slow check skips a beat instead of piling up), stopped
                when the view that owns it goes away.
  ConfirmPolicy one rule for which actions need a confirm step (by verb), so it
                can't drift per-button; documented overrides only.
  Dialog        one modal-dialog helper (was three copy-pasted popups).
  View classes  one per screen; each owns its widgets and its poll jobs.
  App           window, panes, sidebar, routing, tick/watchdog loops.

`khaos-lab --selftest` builds the UI, opens every view, and fails on any Tk
callback error or leaked poll job -- run it after any edit (use xvfb-run so it
doesn't touch your real screen).
"""

